Title: NEON ECHOES
Credit: Written by CinemaLit Studio
Draft: Production Draft

INT. NEON COFFEE SHOP - NIGHT

Flickering cyan neon tubes illuminate rain-streaked windows. MAYA (28, sharp eyes, leather jacket) hunches over a glowing terminal. 

KAI (30s, nervous, trench coat) slides into the vinyl booth opposite her. He places a heavy chrome prop gun wrapped in cloth onto the table.

MAYA
Did you get the drive?

KAI
The cops are monitoring every server in the city, Maya. Vane knows.

MAYA
Then we move fast. Coffee's cold anyway.

EXT. ALLEYWAY BEHIND DINER - NIGHT

Rain falls heavily into puddles reflecting city lights. Maya and Kai hurry toward a battered black picture vehicle parked near the dumpster.

A dark sedan pulls up, blocking the alley exit. DETECTIVE VANE steps out into the pouring rain.

VANE
End of the line, kids. Hand over the drive.

INT. PICTURE VEHICLE - NIGHT

Maya hotwires the ignition. The engine roars. Kai nervously checks the prop gun.

KAI
He's got back-up coming!

MAYA
Hold on tight.

EXT. INDUSTRIAL DOCK - DAY

Dawn breaks over rusted shipping containers. The picture vehicle skids to a halt beside Warehouse 9.

Maya and Kai step out, catching their breath in the morning light.

MAYA
We made it. Now let's upload the evidence before Vane catches up.

INT. ABANDONED WAREHOUSE - DAY

Dust motes float in sunlight beams breaking through high windows. Maya plugs the drive into a portable satellite relay station.

Progress bar reaches 100%. A green chime rings out.

KAI
It's live. The whole world knows the truth.

Maya closes her laptop with a smile.

FADE OUT.
